parameters.text:
=Write 5 Facebook ad copy variants for A/B testing.

Product: {{ $json.product }}
Target audience: {{ $json.target_audience }}
Core pain point: {{ $json.pain_point }}
Offer: {{ $json.offer }}
CTA: {{ $json.cta }}
Objective: {{ $json.objective }}

Write one ad in each of these proven frameworks:
1. PAS (Problem → Agitate → Solution)
2. AIDA (Attention → Interest → Desire → Action)
3. Social Proof (results-first, then offer)
4. Fear of Missing Out (urgency + scarcity)
5. Story (micro-narrative, 3 sentences)

For each variant also write:
- Primary text (main ad body, under 125 words)
- Headline (under 40 chars)
- Description (under 30 chars)

Return JSON:
{
  "variants": [
    {
      "framework": "PAS",
      "primary_text": "",
      "headline": "",
      "description": "",
      "hook_strength": "strong/medium/weak",
      "best_for": "cold/warm/retargeting audience"
    }
  ],
  "recommended_test_order": ["framework names in order to test"]
}

parameters.jsCode:
const raw = $input.item.json.text.replace(/```json|```/g,'').trim();
const data = JSON.parse(raw);
return [{ json: { ...data, brief: $('Extract Brief').item.json } }];

